{
  "_comment": [
    "Bold spans the non-Latin locales keep in the Latin alphabet.",
    "Almost nothing needs listing here: asked to translate the sentence around",
    "it, the engine already keeps a title it recognises ('Kind of Blue',",
    "'Double Irish', 'B-29') and renders a name ('Prometheus', 'New York'), and",
    "fix_latin_spans_nonlatin keeps whatever comes back in Latin.",
    "These are the ones it would translate word for word instead: a bomb's code",
    "name is not a small boy, a tax arrangement is not a double Irishman, and a",
    "title already in a third language stays in it.",
    "\"overrides\" corrects what the engine got wrong: a brand read as the thing it is named after (Apple the fruit, Amazon the river), a term rendered word for word (Greek 'crowding outside' for crowding out).",
    "\"keep_in_course\" is for a name that is right in one course and wrong in another: Jupiter is the planet in the astronomy course and a missile in the Cuban missile crisis, and only the planet has a Greek name.",
    "\"baseline\" is the snapshot --audit measures against: every span that is still in Latin after a full run, which is a title, a brand, an acronym or a glossary link the engine rightly left alone. Anything outside it is new, and fails.",
    "The art movements and the Latin binomials below are named in German, Dutch or Latin in every language, and the technical acronyms are written as they are; only a quiz option asked for out of context would translate them."
  ],
